an  aspiring blockbuster with full-on  franchise potential and like so many  young aspiring superstars before him  things didn't quite work out to be fair  that doesn't have much to do with Kitsch  himself the truth is there are not many  people in or out of showbiz who could  tell you exactly what went wrong with  Disney's 2012 tent pole John Carter it  had all the makings of a surefire  family-friendly crowd-pleasing hit  till it got released when John Carter  finally hit theaters in 2012 it did so  behind a middling critical response and  crippling word-of-mouth with the film's  unintentional kam penis most frequently  mentioned as its biggest problem not  surprisingly the film which is nowhere  near as bad as you've heard became one  of the biggest box-office bombs in  Disney history claiming just north of 73  million dollars at u.s. box offices  barely recouping its mammoth budget with  its worldwide take of just over 284  million dollars though it's quite likely  you've seen kitchen one of his  big-screen rolls over the years it's far  more likely you recognize him from his  early days on television Kitsch did  after all feature prominently in one of  the best-loved dramas of the 2000s one  that also proved small screen  adaptations of big-screen successes  aren't always doomed to failure based on  the 2004 film of the same name the TV  show in question is NBC's rousing sports  drama Friday Night Lights if you somehow  slept on the book the movie and the  series Friday Night Lights follows the  travails of a coach and the players of a  powerhouse football program in a small  Texas town among Friday Night Lights  young cast for future stars like Jesse  Plemons Adrianne Palicki and Michael B  Jordan Taylor Kitsch also appeared in 68  of the show's 76 episodes as the roguish  star running back Tim Riggins if we are  being too bold we'd say he was  frequently brilliant on the series  imbuing his stoic character with natural  charisma and hard-earned wisdom even as  he was frequently boozing it up and  generally running amuck all over town of  course if you do recognize Kitsch from  one of his big screen ventures it's  entirely likely that venture came in is  better than the film turn as gambit in  2009's dreadful x-men origins Wolverine  if you happen to recognize kitsch from  another movie however it may well be for  his hilarious appearance in the samuel  l.jackson starring horror tinged camp  fest the world came to know as snakes on  a plane if you managed to miss kitsch in  the film it's because he wasn't actually  in snakes on a plane for very long in  fact his Randy newlywed was one of the  first characters to die fortunately it  was far from the last we'd see of kitsch  as his Waco performance indicates he has  plenty more left in the tank check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite movies and TV shows are come  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

